# --- the new file ---
# AnixOps Control configuration, written by `anix-control config rewrite`
# from /opt/anixops/control/config/config.yaml on 2026-10-13T08:00:00Z.
# Keys and defaults: docs/reference/configuration.md. The root key and the
# secrets it adopted are in data_dir/root.key, not in this file.
domain: panel.example.com
tls:
  mode: external
  cert_file: /opt/anixops/control/config/tls/fullchain.pem
  key_file: /opt/anixops/control/config/tls/privkey.pem
grpc:
  port: 50052
  public_name: grpc.example.com
subscribe_path: link
# Still read until PostgreSQL support ends (M2, P4): the panel keeps its
# database (a PostgreSQL password stays here until then).
database:
  database: /opt/anixops/control/data/v2board.db
  driver: sqlite
  log_level: "warn"
# --- the report ---
New keys:
  domain: panel.example.com (from agent_install.public_url); the panel's name
  tls.mode: external
  tls.cert_file: /opt/anixops/control/config/tls/fullchain.pem (from grpc.tls_cert_file)
  tls.key_file: /opt/anixops/control/config/tls/privkey.pem (from grpc.tls_key_file)
  grpc.port: 50052
  grpc.public_name: grpc.example.com (from agent_install.grpc_target)
  subscribe_path: link (from app.subscribe_path); keeps the subscription links already handed out

Kept:
  database: still read until PostgreSQL support ends (M2, P4): the panel keeps its database (/opt/anixops/control/data/v2board.db)

Dropped:
  admin.email: still read until M2 (P9), not written: creates the first administrator on an empty database until the one-time claim link replaces it
  admin.password: still read until M2 (P9), not written: creates the first administrator on an empty database until the one-time claim link replaces it; keep it out of the file once an administrator exists
  agent_install.cn_mirror_url: still read until M4 (N30), not written: the mainland download mirror of Agent releases, until Control serves the releases itself
  app.api_token: still read until M5 (N9), not written: the legacy shared token of /flow/upload and the internal v2 routes, removed with them; administrators use admin API tokens
  env: Control always runs as production (its only effect was requiring jwt.secret, which is now derived); start a development instance with -debug
  frontend.enable: still read until M2 (P11), not written: serves the web app from frontend.path until the web app is built into the binary
  frontend.path: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the web app's directory until the web app is built into the binary
  frontend.port: still read until M2 (P11), not written: a second plain listener of tls.mode external while listen is unset; config rewrite does not carry it, point the reverse proxy at listen
  grpc.enabled: still read until M2 (P11), not written: turns the gRPC listener on without domain; with domain it always runs
  grpc.host: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the gRPC listener's address, until it listens on every address
  identity.kek: adopted, kept in /var/lib/anix-control/root.key
  jwt.expire: a built-in value (86400 seconds)
  jwt.secret: adopted, kept in /var/lib/anix-control/root.key
  module_runtime.ca_kek: the root key, kept in /var/lib/anix-control/root.key
  plugins.control_execution_enabled: the built-in packages always run; Control starts their hosts at every start
  plugins.control_host_artifact_dir: still read until M2 (P11), not written: where package hosts' files are kept, until the systemd unit gives Control its directories
  plugins.control_host_runtime_dir: still read until M2 (P11), not written: where package hosts' sockets live, until the systemd unit gives Control its runtime directory
  server.host: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the plain listener of tls.mode external while listen is unset; config rewrite does not carry it, set listen
  server.port: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the plain listener of tls.mode external while listen is unset; config rewrite does not carry it, set listen
  server.trusted_proxies: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the reverse proxies of a container deployment; afterwards tls.mode acme trusts none and tls.mode external trusts loopback
  tls.domain: domain comes from agent_install.public_url
  tls.enable: TLS follows tls.mode

Notes:
  tls.mode external: the old file did not use ACME, so a reverse proxy keeps terminating TLS for the web side; its gRPC certificate becomes tls.cert_file
  tls.mode external: point the reverse proxy at 127.0.0.1:8080 for the whole panel (web, /api, subscriptions, /install): it is one listener now
